ation for parachute deploy and to roll over"},{"t":9.24,"text":"to give the radar a better look at the ground."},{"t":14.37,"text":"- [Male Announcer] (indistinct) indicates shoot deploy."},{"t":17.81,"text":"- [Female Announcer] The navigation has confirmed"},{"t":19.38,"text":"that the parachute has deployed"},{"t":20.85,"text":"and we are seeing significant deceleration"},{"t":23.64,"text":"in the velocity."},{"t":24.48,"text":"Her current velocity is 450 meters per second"},{"t":27.77,"text":"at an altitude of about 12 kilometers"},{"t":29.83,"text":"from the surface of Mars."},{"t":33.29,"text":"- [Male Announcer] Heat shield's set."},{"t":34.85,"text":"- [Female Announcer] Perseverance is now slowed"},{"t":36.1,"text":"to subsonic speeds"},{"t":37.68,"text":"and the heat shield has been separated."},{"t":39.63,"text":"This allows both the radar and the cameras"},{"t":42.09,"text":"to get their first look at the surface."},{"t":44.58,"text":"Current velocity is 145 meters per second"},{"t":47.53,"text":"at an altitude of about nine and a half kilometers"},{"t":50.88,"text":"above the surface."},{"t":68.04,"text":"- [Male Announcer] Nav filter converge."},{"t":69.25,"text":"Lastly solution 3.3 meters per second."},{"t":71.23,"text":"Altitude 7.4 kilometers."},{"t":74.26,"text":"- [Female Announcer] Now has radar lock on the ground."},{"t":76.03,"text":"Current velocity is about 100 meters per second,"},{"t":79.45,"text":"6.6 kilometers of the surface."},{"t":86.19,"text":"Perseverance is continuing to descend on the parachute."},{"t":89.1,"text":"We're coming up on the initialization"},{"t":92.39,"text":"of terrain relative navigation"},{"t":94.2,"text":"and subsequently the timing of the landing engines."},{"t":96.93,"text":"Our current velocity is about 90 meters per second"},{"t":100.49,"text":"at an altitude of 4.2 kilometers."},{"t":107.6,"text":"- [Male Announcer] (indistinct)"},{"t":109.02,"text":"- [Female Announcer] We have confirmation"},{"t":109.85,"text":"that the lander vision system has produced a valid solution"},{"t":112.75,"text":"and part of terrain relative navigation."},{"t":115.0,"text":"- [Male Announcer] (indistinct)"},{"t":116.17,"text":"PBA is a nominal."},{"t":117.73,"text":"- [Female Announcer] We have timing of the landing engine."},{"t":126.11,"text":"- [Male Announcer] Back shelf set."},{"t":127.12,"text":"- [Female Announcer] Current velocity"},{"t":127.96,"text":"is 83 meters per second"},{"t":129.69,"text":"at about 2.6 kilometers from the surface of Mars."},{"t":133.63,"text":"We have confirmation that the back shell has separated."},{"t":136.55,"text":"We are currently performing the divert maneuver."},{"t":139.17,"text":"Current velocity is about 75 meters per second"},{"t":141.47,"text":"at an altitude of about a kilometer off the surface of Mars."},{"t":146.13,"text":"- [Male Announcer] Here in 50 Bravo."},{"t":149.25,"text":"- [Female Announcer] We have completed"},{"t":150.37,"text":"our terrain relative navigation."},{"t":152.58,"text":"Current speed is about 30 meters per second."},{"t":155.43,"text":"Altitude of about 300 meters off the surface of Mars."},{"t":161.66,"text":"We have started our constant velocity accordion,"},{"t":164.41,"text":"which means we are conducting the sky crane,"},{"t":167.96,"text":"about to conduct the sky crane maneuver."},{"t":172.5,"text":"Sky crane maneuver has started"},{"t":176.26,"text":"about 20 meters off the surface."},{"t":184.47,"text":"- [Male Announcer] We're getting signals from (indistinct)."},{"t":187.38,"text":"Tango Delta."},{"t":188.99,"text":"- [Female Announcer] Touchdown confirmed"},{"t":191.23,"text":"(crowd cheers)"},{"t":192.06,"text":"Perseverance safely on the surface of Mars"},{"t":194.38,"text":"ready to begin seeking the sands of past life."},{"t":197.6,"text":"(crowd cheers)"}],"clips":{"liftoff.mp4":[[300.0,307.0],[318.0,331.0]],"ascent.mp4":[[1040.0,1056.0],[1116.0,1146.0],[1170.0,1200.0]],"separation.mp4":[[1468.0,1500.0]],"landing.mp4":[[12.0,52.0],[106.0,200.0]]}}